    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence is genuinely balanced at this pivotal technical juncture. AAPL is trading at $174.65, just $0.49 below the 50 SMA ($175.14) that has rejected price for 11 weeks, and remains below both the 50 and 200 SMAs (both declining). While the bull case cites constructive leading indicators (highest volume rally in two months at 101.67M shares, MACD histogram at +0.91, RSI recovering to 56.83, and a 5.2% two-day recovery), the breakout is not yet confirmed and sentiment data is entirely unavailable across all three sources. The near-term risk-reward is roughly 1:1 ($169.85 downside vs. $180.47 upside), which does not justify aggressive positioning. The correct action is to hold and wait for confirmation \u2014 a close above $175.14 on sustained volume would validate the bullish thesis, while a rejection would vindicate the bearish caution.\n\n**Entry Price**: 174.65\n\n**Stop Loss**: 169.85\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain neutral/market-weight position. Do not deploy fresh capital until $175.14 breakout is confirmed. If adding on confirmation, size at roughly half of a full position.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
